# DESCRIPTION

Section 3 describes the devices: one page for each class of device and the files it serves, and one for each driver.

Drivers are processes, not part of the kernel.
devmgr(8) finds the devices on the buses, matches each against the drivers' manifests (`/boot/drv`), starts the driver it names with the device's registers, interrupts and DMA mappings and nothing else, and starts it again if it dies.
A driver serves its device as files, posted in `/srv`, which others mount: a disk as `/srv/disk0`, served to partd(8).

